==== MCU Driver ====
The MCU Driver provides MCU services for Clock and RAM initialization and other MCU specific services.

In order to enable the MCU Driver for XMEGA Family of AVR8 microcontroller the user MUST add the follwing code in the OIL file:

<pre>
...
MCU_DATA = XMEGA {
  ...
  ENABLE_MCU_DRIVER = TRUE { 
    ...
  };
  ...
};
...
</pre>

===== Error checking =====
The MCU Driver offers two levels of error checking, extended status for development phase and standard status for production phase.

The extended status allows for enhanced plausibility checks on calling MCU Driver services. Due to the additional error checking it requires more execution time and memory 
space than the standard version. However, many errors can be found in a test phase. After all errors have been eliminated, the systemcan be recompiled with the standard version.

In order to enable the extended status for MCU Driver the user MUST add the following code into OIL file:

<pre>
...
MCU_DATA = XMEGA {
  ...
  ENABLE_MCU_DRIVER = TRUE { 
    ...
    MCU_STATUS = EXTENDED;
    ...
  };
  ...
};
...
</pre>

===== APIs Selection =====
By default the MCU Driver enables the <code>EE_Mcu_Init()</code> API only. To anable each other API of the MCU Driver the user MUST add the following code into OIL file:

<pre>
...
MCU_DATA = XMEGA {
  ...
  ENABLE_MCU_DRIVER = TRUE { 
    ...
    MCU_DEINIT_API = TRUE;
    MCU_INITCLOCK_API = TRUE;
    MCU_DEINITCLOCK_API = TRUE;
    MCU_GETCLOCKSTATUS_API = TRUE;
    MCU_DISTRIBUTECLOCK_API = TRUE;
    MCU_SETMODE_API = TRUE;
    MCU_GETRESETREASON_API = TRUE;
    MCU_PERFORMRESET_API = TRUE;
    ...
  };
  ...
};
...
</pre>

Where:
* <code>MCU_DEINIT_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_DeInit()</code> API
* <code>MCU_INITCLOCK_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_InitClock()</code> API
* <code>MCU_DEINITCLOCK_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_DeInitClock()</code> API
* <code>MCU_GETCLOCKSTATUS_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_GetClockStatus()</code> API
* <code>MCU_DISTRIBUTECLOCK_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_DistributeClock()</code> API
* <code>MCU_SETMODE_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_SetMode()</code> API
* <code>MCU_GETRESETREASON_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_GetResetReason()</code> API
* <code>MCU_PERFORMRESET_API</code> enables <code>EE_Mcu_PerformReset()</code> API

===== Power Reduction =====
The Power Reduction is used to shutdown unused peripherals.

In order to enable the Power Reduction for MCU Driver the user MUST add the following code into OIL file:

<pre>
...
MCU_DATA = XMEGA {
  ...
  ENABLE_MCU_POWER_REDUCTION = YES {
    PULL_UP = FALSE;
    PORT_OUT = FALSE;
    JTAG = FALSE;
  };
  ...
};
...
</pre>

By default the unused port pins are set as input port pins with a pull-down.
* The user can change the direction of the port pin from input to output changing the <code>PORT_OUT</code> attribute from <code>FALSE</code< to <code>TRUE</code>.
* The user can set a pull-up to unused port pins changing the <code>PULL_UP</code> attribute from <code>FALSE</code< to <code>TRUE</code>.
* The user can disable the JTAG port pins during the sleep mode changing the <code>JTAG</code> attribute from <code>FALSE</code< to <code>TRUE</code>.

